<h2>About The Game engines!</h2>
<p> </p>
<p>We mostly used different variety of game engines which are mostly specific to <em>genre or features </em>that we are trying to do!</p>
<hr>
<p>Games Engines are divided in :</p>
<table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 235.719px;" border="1">
<tbody>
<tr style="height: 187.156px;">
<td style="width: 100%; height: 187.156px;">
<p><strong><em>Specialized Game Engines :</em></strong> This are engines that are specific to the genre that we are making.</p>
<p>We mostly choose this path if the specific game lines up with the specific genre <em>and the mechanics assumption it does</em> out of the get go.</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 48.5625px;">
<td style="width: 100%; height: 48.5625px;"><strong><em>General Game Engines :</em></strong> The 'we can do it all engine' , we mostly used this engine if the <em>genre is mixed and the mechanics are a more complicated one</em>  </td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr>
<p><strong>What is the engines we used exactly?</strong></p>
